</comment><comment id="FF`Nzx.sZZC0|K_0)tAP" x="270.218362669585" y="153.18110195563895" w="451.6915283203125" h="538.8097839355469">1. Make a prediction about what "show string Hello" will do. Write it on your worksheet.

2. Replace the heart icon with the string "Hello"

3. Download the code and make sure it runs on your Microbit device. Does it look the same as the simulator?

4. Change the string to your name 

5. Download your code again and run it on your Microbit device.

6. Choose one of the images on the screen. Try to represent it using the 25 Microbit LEDs. Use the planning sheet to brainstorm before running your code. 

7. Download your completed image to your Microbit device and share your code to the classroom.</comment><block type="device_forever" id="^VrR^;W[8N%mL#8?O1o:" x="191" y="-29"></block><block type="pxt-on-start" id="}s%MQ.#tMDbi)$@ljQ^~" x="0" y="0"></block><block type="basic_show_icon" id="7{r}X3NSt]v:SiNJQrTI" disabled-reasons="pxt_automatic_disabled" x="6" y="134"><field name="i">IconNames.Heart</field><next><block type="device_print_message" id="?jR(RS$dP~QuW*Q=!::m" disabled-reasons="pxt_automatic_disabled"><value name="text"><shadow type="text" id="?7fVUWDG;]:AFQp~zB9m" disabled-reasons="pxt_automatic_disabled"><field name="TEXT">Hello!</field></shadow></value><next><block type="device_show_leds" id="qO-5F53pU#^*]PEM9rps" disabled-reasons="pxt_automatic_disabled"><field name="LEDS">`
